        <div class="col-md-8">
        <strong>Early Versions</strong>
         <p>
          Early versions were extremely basic. I didn't attempt to style much at all. 
          They were also kind of tedious. Basically, they involved a lot of clicking. I showed my brother in law who works in UX design and his comments refelcted that. Basically the site was just drop downs and clicking next.</p>
        </div>
    </div>


     <div class="row align-items-center mb-5">
      
        <div class="col-md-8">
        <strong>The Rise of AI</strong>
         <p>
          I had already been using AI to help me problem solve issues, so it occured to me one day why don't I make the app AI involved. All along I'd been secretly wondering if AI was rendering my app useless--why not just ask Chatgpt to write you an objective? But I thought what if I involved AI in the process but improved it...Adding dropdowns, cards, and selections. The result was a language objective making guide/avatar.</p>

          <p> Learning how to integrate AI into Python Flask was a little bit of a learning curb. After a basic import, I learned how to manipulate the AI by setting things like it's temperature and giving it prompts. It's a bit like stage directions. An example of what I basically ended up with in each route is below. 

             <pre><code>assistant_reply = clean_gpt_response(
                ask_llm(
                    [
                        {"role": "system", "content":
                         "Explain WIDA language domains (Listening, Speaking, Reading, Writing) "
                         "in one short line each. End with one question: "
                         "'Which domain fits your lesson?' Use bullets; ≤8 words per bullet."
                        }
                    ] + chat_history,
                    model="gpt-4",
                    max_tokens=120,
                    temperature=0.2
                )</code></pre>
            
          </p>

        </div>

